  "Question": "In the lottery method, what should be done with the numbers?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Mix them thoroughly before drawing",
    "B": "Arrange them in ascending order and select only those at the front",
    "C": "Select only even numbers",
    "D": "Repeatedly select the same person until satisfied"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Without thorough mixing, a slip's initial position can affect its chance of being drawn. Mix the numbered slips thoroughly before drawing at random to help give each individual an equal chance. Therefore the answer is A.",
